admin-db-help = Read-only database diagnostics. No credentials or message content are displayed.
admin-db-free-help = Reusable SQLite pages stay inside the file after deletions until space is reclaimed.
admin-db-inspect-help = Detailed inspection can take up to 30 seconds. Table sizes include indexes; PostgreSQL row counts are estimates.
admin-db-limited = Some measurements reached the scan limit or are unavailable on this database.
admin-db-orphan-help = These cached bodies have no message row pointing to them. Inspection does not remove them.

admin-db-growth = Database growth
admin-db-growth-alert = Sustained rapid growth detected. Inspect the largest tables and write origins.
admin-db-growth-warming = Collecting a baseline; at least two samples are needed.
admin-db-growth-normal = No sustained rapid growth detected.
admin-db-growth-rate = Recent growth
admin-db-growth-threshold = Alert threshold
admin-db-origin = Write origin
admin-db-writes = Statements
admin-db-input = Input bytes
admin-db-growth-history = Size history
admin-db-write-help = Write activity over the last 15 minutes, for this server process. Input bytes are bound parameter sizes, not disk growth. Affected rows may include rolled-back transactions. Raw SQL, credentials and message content are excluded. History resets on restart.

admin-db-cleanup = Cleanup
admin-db-log-files = Application log files
admin-db-rotate = Rotate now
admin-db-log-help = Apply configured age, file-count and size limits. Rotation uses the configured compression setting; compression may continue in the background.
admin-db-offline-cleanup = Offline database repair
admin-db-offline-help = Run these commands on the deployment host. Preview changes nothing. Apply stops the app, creates a backup and resumes it afterwards. Compaction needs temporary free disk space. Add --skip-backup only to deliberately omit that copy; purging the index requires a rebuild afterwards.
admin-db-preview-command = Preview cleanup
admin-db-apply-command = Apply cleanup
admin-db-copy-command = Copy command
admin-db-command-copied = Command copied.
admin-db-maintenance-requested = Log maintenance requested.

admin-db-history-range = History period
admin-db-history-all = All available
admin-db-history-help = History starts with this server process. The database chart fits its vertical scale; WAL has a separate scale.
admin-db-payload = Text / binary payload
admin-db-columns = Largest columns
admin-db-live-bytes = Referenced cached body bytes
admin-db-analysis-help = Automatic read-only analysis ranks measured storage consumers. Payload excludes indexes and page overhead; unavailable physical sizes do not hide payload measurements.
admin-db-breakdown = What uses the space
admin-db-history-period = { $from } — { $to }

admin-db-background-title = Background database maintenance
admin-db-background-configure = Configure maintenance
admin-db-background-run = Run a batch
admin-db-background-help = Small batches collect unreferenced bodies after a grace period and reclaim eligible SQLite pages. Live mail stays referenced and is preserved. Status resets on restart.
admin-db-background-result = Scanned: { $scanned } · Removed: { $removed } ({ $bytes }) · Reclaimed pages: { $pages }
admin-db-background-conversion = This database needs conversion before incremental reclamation can run. Use online conversion, or preview the offline command without --apply.
admin-db-background-deferred = Maintenance yielded to a busy database, its work budget, or WAL pressure. It will retry automatically.
admin-db-background-next = Next batch: { $time }

admin-resources-title = Resources
admin-resources-help = Read-only resource measurements distinguish effective server capacity, the host and this process.
admin-resources-allocation = Effective server capacity
admin-resources-cpu-cores = Effective CPU cores
admin-resources-memory-limit = Memory limit
admin-resources-memory-available = Available memory headroom
admin-resources-process = Server process
admin-resources-process-memory = Resident memory
admin-resources-process-cpu = CPU usage
admin-resources-cpu-help = 100% CPU means one logical core. A process using several cores can exceed 100%. Renderer helper processes are not included.
admin-resources-cpu-warmup = CPU usage needs two observations. Unavailable measurements are never shown as zero.
admin-resources-host = Host memory
admin-resources-host-total = Host memory total
admin-resources-host-available = Host memory available
admin-resources-filesystem = Data filesystem
admin-resources-filesystem-total = Filesystem capacity
admin-resources-filesystem-available = Filesystem available
admin-resources-filesystem-help = The filesystem containing this server’s data directory. Remote database storage is not included.
admin-resources-poll-help = Updates every 10 seconds while this page is visible.
admin-resources-container = Container isolation detected. Capacity measurements include readable resource limits.

admin-db-online-title = Online SQLite conversion
admin-db-online-help = Builds a new SQLite generation while mail stays online. Database requests may queue briefly during switching. Extra disk space is required; the previous generation is retained.
admin-db-online-start = Start conversion
admin-db-online-cancel = Cancel conversion
admin-db-online-none = No conversion has been started in this server process.
admin-db-online-phase = Stage
admin-db-online-pending = Pending changes
admin-db-online-retained = The previous database generation is retained. Remove it only after verification through a separate maintenance action.
admin-db-online-poll = Checks active conversions every 2 seconds while this page is visible.
admin-db-online-copied-rows = Copied rows
admin-db-online-copied-bytes = Copied bytes
admin-db-online-cancel-unavailable = Cancellation is no longer available at this stage.
admin-db-online-phase-preparing = Preparing
admin-db-online-phase-copying = Copying data
admin-db-online-phase-verifying = Verifying the copy
admin-db-online-phase-catching-up = Applying recent changes
admin-db-online-phase-waiting-for-cutover = Waiting to switch
admin-db-online-phase-switching = Switching database
admin-db-online-phase-publishing = Publishing the new generation
admin-db-online-phase-recovery-required = Recovery review required
admin-db-online-phase-completed = Completed
admin-db-online-phase-cancelled = Cancelled
admin-db-online-phase-failed = Failed

admin-resources-cpu-capabilities = CPU capabilities
admin-resources-cpu-architecture = Architecture
admin-resources-cpu-kernel = Selected kernel for large inputs
admin-resources-cpu-features = Available CPU features
admin-resources-cpu-portable = Portable
admin-resources-cpu-kernel-help = Applies to ASCII lowercasing. AVX2 starts at { $avx2 } bytes and AVX-512 at { $avx512 } bytes when supported. Short inputs use the portable path. Available features are not all used by the app.

admin-db-pool-demand-help = Connections grow with demand and shrink when idle, within the displayed minimum and maximum.
admin-db-pool-restart-help = Connection limits and timings change only after a full server restart; this is not live ceiling resizing.
admin-db-pool-acquisitions = Pool acquisitions
admin-db-pool-acquire-failures = Acquisition failures
admin-db-pool-total-wait = Cumulative acquisition time
admin-db-pool-max-wait = Longest acquisition time
admin-db-pool-reads = Measured reads
admin-db-pool-writes = Measured writes
admin-db-pool-operation-help = Counters cover this server process’s measured query helpers. Direct SQLx calls and other replicas are excluded.
admin-db-sampled-help = Values marked ≥ are measured lower bounds from up to 512 rows, not estimated totals. Exact scans reached their time limit.
admin-db-physical-limited = Physical scan limited
admin-db-body-help = Bodies cache encrypted raw messages, including inline images and attachments. Referenced bodies still belong to messages; orphaned bodies have no message link. Payload bytes differ from allocated or reusable file pages.

admin-db-retained-title = Retained databases
admin-db-retained-help = Old database copies retained after online conversion. Only the verified previous generation is eligible. Keep an independent backup before deleting.
admin-db-retained-empty = No verified retained database is available.
admin-db-retained-modified = Last modified
admin-db-retained-actions = Actions
admin-db-retained-delete = Delete { $file }
admin-db-retained-confirm-title = Delete retained database?
admin-db-retained-confirm-body = Permanently delete { $file } ({ $size })? This recovery copy will be removed. Keep a verified independent backup.
admin-db-retained-confirm = Delete database copy
admin-db-retained-deleted = Deleted retained database { $file }.
admin-db-retained-busy = Database maintenance is running. Try again after it finishes.
admin-db-retained-sidecars = SQLite recovery files are still present. Close other database tools and review recovery before deleting.
admin-db-retained-unavailable = This copy could not be verified for deletion.
